@startuml
title RubyGYM - Selected Use Cases

left to right direction
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam ArrowColor #374151
skinparam actor {
  BorderColor #334155
  BackgroundColor #F8FAFC
  FontColor #111827
}
skinparam rectangle {
  BorderColor #991B1B
  BackgroundColor #FFFFFF
  FontColor #111827
}
skinparam usecase {
  BorderColor #991B1B
  BackgroundColor #FFFFFF
  FontColor #111827
}
skinparam note {
  BorderColor #B45309
  BackgroundColor #FFFBEB
  FontColor #111827
}

actor "Admin" as Admin
actor "Trainer" as Trainer
actor "Member" as Member

rectangle "RubyGYM System" {
  usecase "UC01 Manage Members" as UC01
  usecase "UC02 Register/Renew Subscription Plan" as UC02
  usecase "UC03 Create Training Session" as UC03
  usecase "UC04 View Personal Schedule" as UC04
  usecase "UC05 Perform Monthly Evaluation" as UC05
  usecase "UC06 Set Training Goal" as UC06
}

Admin -- UC01
Member -- UC02
Admin -- UC02
Trainer -- UC03
Admin -- UC03
Member -- UC04
Trainer -- UC05
Admin -- UC05
Member -- UC06

note right of UC03
Member is not an actor for this use case.
Trainer creates sessions for assigned members.
Admin can create sessions through the API.
end note

note right of UC05
Trainer or Admin can perform the evaluation.
Member only views evaluation results.
Evaluation reads Member's saved training goal
when target values are available.
end note

note bottom of UC06
Only the Member creates/edits their own goal
(single source of truth). Trainer and Admin
read it but cannot modify it (ADR-001).
The goal is set on the Goals page, not during
onboarding (ADR-002).
end note

@enduml
